## How It Works

Five training days. Each one follows the same order: **warmup → plyo/power → strength → conditioning**. Power work comes first while you're fresh. Never do jumps or sprints fatigued.

**Suggested week:** Day 1 Mon · Day 2 Tue · Rest Wed · Day 3 Thu · Day 4 Fri · Day 5 Sat · Rest Sun

### Intensity Key

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| **RIR** | Reps in reserve. 2 RIR = stop with 2 clean reps left. |
| **RPE** | Effort out of 10. RPE 8 ≈ 2 reps left. |
| **Top set** | Heaviest set of the day. Work up to an **RPE 8**. Rest 3–4 min after. |
| **Ramp-up** | Warmup sets into the top set: ~45% × 5, 60% × 3, 75% × 2, 85% × 1 (of top-set weight). |
| **CAT** | Compensatory Acceleration Training. Lighter load, moved as fast as possible every rep. If bar speed drops, end the set. |
| **Zone 2** | Easy steady cardio. You can hold a conversation. Roughly 60–70% of max heart rate. |

### Progression

- **Top sets:** When you hit your reps at RPE 7 or easier, add 5–10 lb (lower body) or 2.5–5 lb (upper body) next week.
- **Back-offs & speed work:** Calculated from that day's top set. Speed is the goal; never grind these.
- **Accessories:** Double progression. Hit the top of the rep range on every set at 2 RIR, then add load.
- **Deload:** Every 6th week, cut sets by ~40% and skip top sets.

