## Day 1 — Caladan: Knee-Dominant & Horizontal Power

*Home soil. The foundation day: a heavy squat to wake up the nervous system, then speed.*

**Warmup (8–10 min)**

- 90/90 hip switch — 6/side
- Cossack squat — 6/side
- Single-leg glute bridge — 8/side
- Copenhagen plank — 30s/side

**Plyo / Potentiation**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Extensive ankle pogos | 2 × 20 | Short contacts, stiff ankles |
| Broad jump | 2 × 3 | Max distance, walk back and fully reset |
| Single-leg lateral plant to hop, use slantboard if possible | 2 × 3/side | Stick briefly, explode back |

**Strength**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| High-bar back squat | Ramp-up → 1 × 4 | Top set, RPE 8 |
| Squat speed back-offs (CAT) | 5 × 2 | ~70% of top set, max bar speed, 60–75s rest |
| DB incline press | 3 × 8 | 2 RIR |
| Lateral raise | 3 × 12 | 2 RIR |
| Supported dead hang | 3 × 30s | Feet on a box, knees at 90° |

**Conditioning:** 20 min incline walk + 20 min bike (Zone 2)

---

## Day 2 — Crysknife: Upper Push & Elastic Upper Body

*Sharp and fast. Explosive pressing, then controlled hypertrophy work.*

**Warmup (6–8 min)**

- Quadruped serratus push-up — 10
- Half-kneeling shoulder CAR — 8 forward, 8 back
- Band pull-apart — 12
- Plank — 30s

**Plyo**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Explosive rebound push-up | 3 × 5 | Hands leave the floor, minimal ground contact |

**Strength**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cambered bar incline press | Ramp-up → 1 × 3 | Top set, RPE 8 |
| Incline press back-offs | 3 × 6 | Drop ~10–15% from top set, 2 RIR |
| Cable neutral-grip row | 3 × 6 | Sharp pull, controlled eccentric |
| **Superset A1:** Incline DB curl | 3 × 8 | 2 RIR |
| **Superset A2:** Skull crusher | 3 × 12 | 2 RIR |

**Conditioning:** 25–30 min incline walk or easy bike (Zone 2)

---

## Day 3 — Sardaukar: Posterior Chain & Triple Extension

*The brute day. Heaviest pull of the week, built on violent hips.*

**Warmup (8–10 min)**

- Cat-camel — 8
- Bird dog — 4/side, 5s hold
- Wall ankle rocks — 8/side
- Bodyweight hip hinge drill — 6

**Power**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hardstyle KB swing (light) | 3 × 6 | Violent hip snap, reset each rep |

**Strength**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Trap bar deadlift | Ramp-up → 1 × 3 | Top set, RPE 8 |
| Trap bar speed pulls (CAT) | 4 × 3 | ~70–75% of top set, dead stop each rep, max speed off the floor |
| Weighted dip | 4 × 6 | 2 RIR |
| Chest-supported row | 3 × 8–10 | 2 RIR |
| Standing calf raise | 3 × 12–15 | Full stretch at the bottom, 2 RIR |
| Pallof press | 3 × 10/side | Resist rotation, don't rush |

**Conditioning:** 30 min Zone 2

---

## Day 4 — Sandrider: Sprint Acceleration, Rotational Power & Upper Pull

*Speed, rotation, and grip. Everything you'd need to mount a worm.*

**Warmup (10–12 min)**

- Leg swings — 15 front/back + 15 lateral per leg
- Thoracic rotation — 8/side
- Wall acceleration march — 2 × 6 switches/leg
- Tall-to-short snap-down — 2 × 6
- Progressive build-ups — 2 × 30 yd at 60–70%

**Plyo & Sprints**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rotational med-ball scoop / shot-put throw | 3 × 4/side | 6–8 lb ball, max release speed |
| Sprint accelerations | 3 × 15–20 yd | 2-point stance, 80–90% effort, full walk-back (90–120s) |

**Strength**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kneeling landmine press | Ramp-up → 1 × 4–5 | Top set, RPE 8 |
| Landmine press back-offs | 3 × 6 | Drop ~20% from top set, 2 RIR |
| Pull-up or lat pulldown | 3 × 6–8 | Slow and controlled, 2 RIR |
| Face pull | 3 × 15 | 2 RIR |
| Farmer carry | 3 × 40 yd | Heavy; straps allowed |

**Alactic Conditioning:** Prowler push/pull or bike sprints — 4–5 rounds of 10s max effort, 75–90s passive rest

---

## Day 5 — Weirding Way: Unilateral Integrity & Elastic Deceleration

*Balance, control, and landing. Strength that holds up on one leg.*

**Warmup (8–10 min)**

- Quadruped adductor rockback — 6/side
- Standing ankle CAR — 6/side
- Reverse lunge to single-leg balance — 5/side
- Low single-leg hops — 20/side

**Plyo**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Low-box depth drop | 3 × 4 | 12–18" box, step off, stick the landing instantly |
| Single-leg bounds | 2 × 4/side | Immediate bounce off the ground |

**Strength (strict 2 RIR throughout)**

| Exercise | Sets × Reps | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bulgarian split squat | 3 × 8/leg | |
| Seated hamstring curl | 2 × 12 | |
| Leg extension | 2 × 12 | Slow eccentric |
| Single-leg standing calf raise | 3 × 10/side | |
| **Superset A1:** Reverse fly | 3 × 10–12 | 30s rest between exercises |
| **Superset A2:** Seated hammer curl | 3 × 10 | |

**Conditioning:** 25 min incline walk (Zone 2)

